flowchart TB
  accTitle: Engineering Activity Portfolio architecture
  accDescr: On this machine, an hourly collector reads local hooks and logs from Claude Code, Codex, and Cursor plus the public GitHub contribution calendar, and reduces them to dates and counts. Prompts, code, filenames, and repository names never leave the machine. The validated snapshot is published to a public activity feed in the repository. GitHub Actions runs the tests and privacy check, builds the static export, and deploys it to GitHub Pages. Visitors' browsers load the static site and poll the feed for a newer day. The contact form and blog editor go through a Cloudflare Worker.

  subgraph machine["THIS MACHINE · PROMPTS, CODE, NAMES STAY HERE"]
    tools["`**Coding tools**
    Claude Code, Codex, Cursor`"]
    collector["`**Hourly collector**
    dates + counts only`"]
  end

  calendar["`**GitHub calendar**
  public contributions`"]

  subgraph github["GITHUB"]
    feed[("`**activity.json**
    public feed`")]
    actions["`**Actions**
    tests, privacy check, build`"]
    pages["`**Pages**
    static export`"]
  end

  browser(["`**Visitor's browser**`"])
  worker["`**Cloudflare Worker**
  contact form, blog editor`"]

  tools -->|hooks, local logs| collector
  calendar --> collector
  collector ==>|validated snapshot| feed
  feed ==> actions
  actions ==> pages
  pages ==> browser
  browser -.->|polls for a newer day| feed
  browser -.-> worker

